    "result_text": "The suite is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required an owner's `riskFlag` to be `true` when **any** of three conditions hold \u2014 possible duplicate, disposable-adjacent email domain, or city over its soft capacity \u2014 else `false`. This is a derived field on the owner response, following the same convention the codebase already uses for computed fields (`locality`, `ownerSegment`, `identityKey`, \u2026): declared in the OpenAPI schema and computed via a mapper expression.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` at build time).\n\n2. **`DisposableEmail.java`** (new) \u2014 centralizes disposable-domain knowledge:\n   - `isBlocked(domain)` \u2014 exact blocklist match (the existing hard-reject behavior).\n   - `isAdjacent(email)` \u2014 the new \"disposable-**adjacent**\" notion: the domain's second-level label matches a known disposable domain's base label, so subdomains (`inbox.mailinator.com`) and sibling suffixes (`mailinator.net`) count, while a plain `example.test` does not.\n\n3. **`OwnerRiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 `forOwner(owner)` = `possibleDuplicate` OR disposable-adjacent email OR `capacityWarning` (the city's soft-capacity signal, set at creation when the city already held \u226540 owners, below the hard limit of 50). Null-safe via `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`.\n\n4. **`RequireOwnerFields.java`** \u2014 refactored the inline disposable-domain set to delegate to `DisposableEmail.isBlocked(...)`, keeping the two levels of matching (hard-reject vs. soft-flag) in one place. Behavior unchanged.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` mapping expression.\n\nThe `riskFlag` is purely derived from the stored owner, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` reflects the same value assigned at creation. The provided acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`, a unique owner with no email \u2192 `riskFlag` false) passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
